      "type": "practice",
      "subtopic": "Batch 3 · Detailed Solutions",
      "question": "The cost of $5$ kg potatoes is ₹$75$. Find the cost of $8$ kg. Also: with a fixed budget of ₹$75$, if price rises from ₹$15$/kg to ₹$25$/kg, how many kg can be bought?",
      "answer": "₹$120$ for 8 kg; $3$ kg at ₹$25$/kg with fixed ₹$75$ budget",
      "options": [],
      "glassboxSteps": [
        {
          "rule": "Direct (cost vs kg)",
          "why": "Cost per kg = 75/5.",
          "math": "15 \\times 8 = 120"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Inverse (budget fixed)",
          "why": "Quantity × price = constant budget.",
          "math": "75 / 25 = 3 \\text{ kg}"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "8 kg costs ₹120; at ₹25/kg, ₹75 buys 3 kg.",
      "linked_note_id": "CH09-sec-direct-and-inverse-variation",
      "source": "practice-session"
    },
